Short:        UTF-8 Unicode text editor with Emoji for AmigaOS 3.9/3.2
Author:       krabobmkd
Uploader:     victorien.ferry@free.fr
Type:         text/edit
Version:      0.9
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 3.9
Requires:     68020, AmigaOS 3.9 or 3.2.x, 8 MB Fast RAM


EmojiGear is a UTF-8 Unicode text editor for AmigaOS 3.9 or 3.2.x (68020+).
It renders TrueType/OpenType fonts via a built-in FreeType 2 engine and
displays full-colour Emoji from CBDT/CBLC bitmap fonts -- on real 68k
hardware.  Multiple documents open in a tab bar.  Load and save UTF-8,
ISO Latin-1, ISO Latin-2; auto-detect UTF-16.  Find & Replace, Undo/
Redo, word wrap, ANSI escape rendering, configurable font size, and an
Emoji Box mapping 40 glyphs to F-key combinations.

Beyond the editor, the package installs three reusable Amiga components
that any developer can open from their own application:
  utf8rastport.library  -- FreeType 2 Unicode rendering on any RastPort,
                          with font fallback chains and colour Emoji.
  unitexteditor.gadget  -- the full editor as a BOOPSI gadget class,
                          embeddable in any application window.
  unibutton.gadget      -- a push-button gadget with Unicode/Emoji labels.

All settings are stored in the icon Tooltypes.  A standard Amiga
Installer script handles everything, including a choice of low-colour
(OCS/ECS) or high-quality (AGA/RTG) default configuration.

---------------------------------------------------------------------------

EmojiGear v0.9

---------------------------------------------------------------------------

WHAT IS IT?

EmojiGear is a UTF-8 Unicode text editor for AmigaOS 3.9 or 3.2.x, running on any
Amiga with a 68020 or better processor.  It renders TrueType and OpenType
fonts using a built-in FreeType 2 engine, and displays full-colour Emoji
from a CBDT/CBLC colour bitmap font.  On a 68k Amiga.  Yes, really.

It opens, edits, and saves plain text files in UTF-8, ISO Latin-1, and
ISO Latin-2 encoding, handles UTF-16 on load, and can export as
backslash-escaped ASCII for maximum portability.  Multiple documents can
be open simultaneously in a tab bar.  ANSI escape sequences are rendered
for coloured terminal output and log files.

Beyond the application itself, EmojiGear ships three reusable Amiga
shared components that any developer can use in their own programs:

  utf8rastport.library
    A standard AmigaOS shared library that brings FreeType 2 glyph
    rendering to any RastPort.  Manages font fallback chains, glyph
    caches, anti-aliasing, colour Emoji, and CLUT/RTG colour mapping.

  unitexteditor.gadget
    A BOOPSI gadget class providing the full Unicode text editor widget,
    embeddable in any BOOPSI-aware application window.

  unibutton.gadget
    A BOOPSI push-button gadget that renders its label with FreeType,
    enabling Unicode and Emoji text in button labels.

---------------------------------------------------------------------------

FEATURES

- Full UTF-8 editing: type, paste, save any Unicode character, including
  Emoji, CJK, Greek, Cyrillic, Arabic and more.
- TrueType / OpenType font rendering via FreeType 2.
- Full-colour Emoji from CBDT/CBLC fonts (e.g. NotoColorEmoji).
- Font fallback chain: combine a text font with an Emoji font and they
  both work seamlessly in the same line of text.
- Multi-document tab bar (up to 20 open documents).
- Load / save in UTF-8, ISO Latin-1 (western), ISO Latin-2 (central/
  eastern European).  Auto-detects UTF-16 (BE and LE) on load.
- Find & Replace with case-insensitive option.
- Undo / Redo history.
- ANSI escape sequence rendering (Amiga pen mode and Unix/xterm 256-
  colour mode).
- Word wrap, force monospace, configurable tab width.
- Adjustable font size at runtime (Ctrl++ / Ctrl+-).
- Emoji Box window: 40 Emoji assignable to F-key combinations.
- Font settings window: configure up to 3 text fonts + 1 Emoji font.
- Settings window: colours, tab behaviour, screen mode.
- All settings saved in icon Tooltypes (EmojiGear.info).
- Iconifiable to Workbench backdrop.
- Opens files from CLI: EmojiGear file1.txt file2.txt [Latin1|Latin2]
- AmigaGuide documentation included.

---------------------------------------------------------------------------

REQUIREMENTS

- Amiga with 68020 or better CPU
- AmigaOS 3.9 or 3.2.x
- At least 8 MB Fast RAM (more is better for large files and Emoji fonts)
- At least 32 kB stack (set via the icon or: stack 32768)
- For colour Emoji and antialiased text: AGA or an RTG card
  (Picasso96 / CyberGraphX) with 8-bit or better screen depth

---------------------------------------------------------------------------

INSTALLATION

Double-click the Install icon and follow the on-screen instructions.
The installer will:
  - Ask where to install EmojiGear
  - Install utf8rastport.library to Libs:
  - Install unitexteditor.gadget and unibutton.gadget to
    SYS:Classes/Gadgets/  (skipped if a newer version is already present)
  - Install four TrueType fonts to Fonts:
      LiberationSans-Regular.ttf   (proportional text)
      UbuntuMono-Regular.ttf       (monospace text)
      NotoColorEmoji32.ttf         (colour Emoji, compact 32px strikes)
      OpenMoji-black-glyf.ttf      (2-colour Emoji, works on any depth)
  - Optionally install example text files (UTF-8, Latin-1, Latin-2,
    ANSI colour, UTF-16, multilingual)
  - Ask whether you prefer a low-colour (OCS/ECS) or high-quality
    (AGA/RTG) default configuration

To start EmojiGear, double-click its icon in the installed drawer.

